dium", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts governor is one of the safest Democratic holds on the 2026 map. Incumbent Maura Healey faces Republican Mike Minogue and independent Andrea James in a state that backed Democrats by 14 points in recent cycles. Polling has been remarkably stable all year: Suffolk's October survey showed Healey up 59-36, UMass Amherst had her ahead 56-31, and earlier fall polls showed similar 20-plus-point margins. All eight expert raters, from Cook to Sabato, place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets price Healey's win odds at 97 to 98 percent.\n\nMinogue has spent the final weeks attacking Healey's honesty and tying her to national issues, while she campaigns on her record and opposition to Trump. Super PACs are active in the closing days, but no evidence suggests the race is competitive; the only real question is the size of Healey's victory margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin"